dzn: Make block-texel views of several layers or levels null instead of losing the device

Vulkan lets a block-compressed image created with
VK_IMAGE_CREATE_BLOCK_TEXEL_VIEW_COMPATIBLE_BIT be viewed in an
uncompressed format of the block's size, such as an R32G32B32A32_UINT view
of a BC3 image, over any number of array layers. Direct3D 12 casts a
compressed resource to an uncompressed format only in a view of one mip
level and one layer, and answers other views by removing the device, which
loses every Vulkan device on it. gfxstream's GPU texture decoder made such a
view of all six faces of a BC3 cube map (dEQP-GLES31 copy_image of ASTC cube
maps, RTX 4080 Laptop GPU under WSL2), and the Android VM went down.

Create a shader resource or unordered access view of that kind as a null
descriptor: reads return zero and writes are dropped, and Dozen logs one
warning. Other views are unchanged.

